From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:01:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Bravery: allow 64-bit-only stable builds

Chromium's binary-size expectation checks reference the 32-bit and
64/32-bit Trichrome and WebView variants, which only exist with
enable_android_secondary_abi. Skip them when it's off, so a 64-bit-only
build (all a Pixel 7 or later can run) passes gn gen.
---
 .../android/expectations/expectations.gni.yaml | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 rewrite/chrome/android/expectations/expectations.gni.yaml

diff --git a/rewrite/chrome/android/expectations/expectations.gni.yaml b/rewrite/chrome/android/expectations/expectations.gni.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..2edd5b07d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rewrite/chrome/android/expectations/expectations.gni.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Copyright (c) 2026 The Bravery Authors. All rights reserved.
+# This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
+# License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this file,
+# You can obtain one at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
+
+substitutions:
+  - description: |
+      Bravery: allow 64-bit-only stable builds
+
+      The binary-size expectation checks reference the 32-bit and 64/32-bit
+      Trichrome and WebView variants, which only exist when
+      enable_android_secondary_abi is on. Bravery builds 64-bit only (modern
+      Pixels can't run 32-bit code), so skip those checks then; otherwise
+      `gn gen` fails with unresolved dependencies.
+    count: 2
+    regex:
+      pattern: 'android_channel == "stable")'
+      replace: 'android_channel == "stable") && enable_android_secondary_abi'
